{# Widget: images. One turns into a single frame, several into a slider, which
   is what `_image_slider` already does for every block that shows images.

   `media_selection` is stored as `{ids: [...]}` and resolved to a plain list at
   render time, but not in every context, so the field is normalised here rather
   than in each caller. Handing the raw shape to the slider makes it resolve the
   list itself as if it were one id, which fails in the database layer with an
   error naming neither the template nor the field. #}
{% set imageList = images|default([]) %}
{% set imageList = imageList.ids|default(imageList) %}

{#- The radius is carried here, on a wrapper, because the slider deliberately
    owns none: it expects the consuming template to round and clip it, which is
    what `text_images` does with its own image wrapper. This widget had no such
    wrapper, so "Image radius" reached the slider and stopped there - the one
    widget of the catalogue ignoring the setting, while the video and the map
    both honour it through a wrapper of their own.

    `overflow-hidden` goes with the radius and only with it: the corners belong
    to the frame, and the slides inside are absolutely positioned. -#}
{% set wrapRadius = imageRadius|default('') %}

<div class="iw-widget__image-wrap{% if wrapRadius %} {{ wrapRadius }} overflow-hidden{% endif %}">
    {% include '@ItechWorldSuluTailwindTheme/blocks/common/_image_slider.html.twig' with {
        images: imageList,
        imageFormat: imageFormat|default('iw_theme_16_9'),
        showName: showName|default(false),
        autoplay: true,
        aspectRatio: aspectRatio|default('16/9'),
        imageRadius: imageRadius|default('')
    } only %}
</div>
